      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\n#13397 added the CPU shm kernels `shm_allgather_into_tensor` and `shm_reduce_scatter_tensor` to sgl-kernel. #12961 routed CPU through `GroupCoordinator._all_gather_into_tensor` / `_reduce_scatter_tensor`, but left `TODO: add optimized ... kernel for cpu` and never called those kernels. So on CPU, the DP attention gather/scatter still went through `torch.distributed` (gloo).\r\n\r\nThis PR routes `all_gather_into_tensor` and `reduce_scatter_tensor` to shm kernels.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- `distributed/parallel_state.py`\r\n  - `_all_gather_into_tensor`: on CPU, call `sgl_kernel.shm_allgather_into_tensor` when `is_shm_available(dtype, world_size, local_size)` holds.\r\n  - `_reduce_scatter_tensor`: on CPU, call `sgl_kernel.shm_reduce_scatter_tensor(..., REDUCE_OP_SUM)` under the same condition.\r\n  - Remove the two TODOs left by #12961.\r\n  - If the condition does not hold (no AMX or arm64, dtype outside bf16/fp16/fp32, or multi-node), fall back to gloo as before.\r\n- `model_executor/cpu_graph_runner.py`: register fake impls for both ops. They mutate `output` in place and return nothing, like `shm_allreduce`, so `--enable-torch-compile` works on CPU.\r\n\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39237653425](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39237653425)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39237653644](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39237653644)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39237653400](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39237653400)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
